.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt COOK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cook
.Nd rebuild the next and seen merge branches
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
rebuilds two merge branches in a
.Xr jj 1
repository, in the style of git.git's integration branches.
Topics flow from
.Sy seen
to
.Sy next
to trunk.
.Pp
The description of the
.Sy next
commit lists the topics of both branches, one per line, below a line
that reads
.Li [cook] .
Text above that line is free prose, such as a title and notes.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
next <ref>
seen <ref>
.Ed
.Pp
A
.Ar ref
is any revision that names a topic: a local bookmark, a remote
bookmark such as
.Li foo@origin ,
or a change id.
It is resolved each time
.Nm
runs, so a topic follows its bookmark as the bookmark moves.
.Pp
.Nm
rebases
.Sy next
onto
.Li trunk()
and each
.Sy next
topic, in the order listed.
It then rebases
.Sy seen
onto
.Sy next
and each
.Sy seen
topic.
A branch with no topics sits on its base alone.
After each rebase,
.Nm
removes the branch's redundant parents.
A topic that has landed on trunk is dropped, and so is a base that a
topic already contains.
A topic listed under both
.Sy next
and
.Sy seen
is merged into
.Sy next
only.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Print the
.Xr jj 1
commands instead of running them.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It fails, and changes nothing, if the description of
.Sy next
has no
.Li [cook]
line, or if a line below it is not blank and is not a
.Li next
or
.Li seen
line with exactly one
.Ar ref .
.Sh EXAMPLES
A description of
.Sy next
that merges one local and one remote topic, and stages a third topic
in
.Sy seen :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
next

[cook]
next fix-parser
next feature@origin
seen experiment
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jj 1
